                    r2_novelty_label:       `Target idea-novelty score for your shortlist of 3 (1 = generic, 5 = non-obvious to an informed rival)`,
                    r2_novelty_readout:     `Novelty bar you commit to:`,
                    r2_novelty_of:          `/ 5`,
                    r2_novelty_hint:        `A high bar with no human judgment behind it is just a number. AI supercharges structure — it doesn't replace the human who filters for genuine novelty and field-truth.`,
                    mode_divergent:         `Divergent — use AI to blow open the option space (new customers, models, wedge features), then human-filter for novelty & feasibility`,
                    mode_convergent:        `Convergent — humans generate a shortlist, then use AI to red-team and stress-test it`,
                    mode_synthetic:         `Synthetic-customer — use AI to simulate buyer objections before spending real validation budget`,
                    mode_oracle:            `Take the AI's answer — prompt it for 40 ideas, shortlist the top 5 it ranks, ship those`,
                    human_judgment:         `Field-truth judgment — we know which "obvious" idea every founder with this prompt also got, and cut it for a non-obvious wedge only an insider would see`,
                    human_polish:           `Better prompts and prettier slides — we package the AI output more cleanly`,
                    human_nothing:          `Nothing specific — the AI's ranking is good enough; speed is our edge`,

                    r3_alloc_label:         `Allocate the fixed C$25,000 / 4-week validation budget to retire the most risk per dollar (must total C$25k)`,
                    r3_total_readout:       `Validation budget allocated:`,
                    r3_total_cap:           `/ C$25k`,
                    r3_spread_label:        `Concentrate the budget on one beachhead, or spread it across the candidate markets?`,
                    r3_signal_label:        `The interviews surface a signal card: plant owners say "nice to have"; quality managers say "I have budget and I'm measured on defect escape rates." What do you do?`,
                    alloc_interviews:       `15 problem interviews — C$3k each block (low cost, medium signal, surfaces the real buyer)`,
